1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:04,267
In this lesson, you'll make your
circle move with the arrow keys.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:06,520
We start where lesson one ended:

3
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:08,100
the player is a teal circle,

4
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:09,660
in the middle of the screen.

5
00:00:10,067 --> 00:00:13,527
Open Control, and drag forever
under look like a circle.

6
00:00:13,987 --> 00:00:16,927
Everything inside forever
runs again, every frame.

7
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:20,713
From Control again, drag if
then into the forever loop.

8
00:00:21,067 --> 00:00:24,847
From Sensing, drag key right arrow
pressed into the slot of the if.

9
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,260
Then from Motion, drag change x by,

10
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,240
inside the if, and make it 3.

11
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:31,713
So, if the right arrow key is pressed,

12
00:00:31,893 --> 00:00:34,593
x grows by 3, and the
circle moves right.

13
00:00:34,933 --> 00:00:36,633
Left is almost the same.

14
00:00:37,113 --> 00:00:39,633
Copy the if with
control C and control V,

15
00:00:39,713 --> 00:00:42,033
put the copy underneath,
pick left arrow,

16
00:00:42,073 --> 00:00:43,353
and type minus 3.

17
00:00:44,233 --> 00:00:46,093
Up and down change y instead.

18
00:00:46,573 --> 00:00:48,193
Drag another if under the others,

19
00:00:48,233 --> 00:00:50,313
put key pressed in
it, and pick up arrow.

20
00:00:50,733 --> 00:00:53,213
Then add change y by, with minus 3.

21
00:01:00,733 --> 00:01:02,613
In the game, y grows downwards,

22
00:01:02,693 --> 00:01:04,233
so minus 3 goes up.

23
00:01:04,453 --> 00:01:06,713
One more copy for down arrow, with 3.

24
00:01:14,167 --> 00:01:15,827
Now press Run, and click the game,

25
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,247
so it gets the keys.

26
00:01:17,667 --> 00:01:20,467
The arrow keys move your
circle around the screen.

27
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:25,427
In the code, each if became
an IF with a key test,

28
00:01:25,587 --> 00:01:27,827
inside the LOOP that runs every frame.

29
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:28,940
Great work!

30
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:31,620
In lesson three, you'll
catch a coin and keep score.
